{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "Capt. Morgan, my inspection found that Truck 18's powered cargo inverter is unavailable, while Truck 12's current payload certification is exactly six pallets. The inspection result is still being entered in the motor-pool system, so it hasn't propagated yet. Both trucks are otherwise operational. This means the normal assignment won't work — the temperature-sensitive clinic supplies need a functioning inverter, and Truck 18 can't provide that right now. The correct reassignment is: Truck 12 takes the four pallets of clinic supplies, which are within its six-pallet certification and can use its operational inverter, and Truck 18 takes the six pallets of generator repair parts, which do not require powered refrigeration. The dispatch plan must also include a maintenance/repair request for Truck 18's inverter as a committed action item."}
```

